# Fingerprints gitleaks must not report again, one per line, in the form
#   <commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>
# exactly as `make lint` prints it (the finding line ends with "Fingerprint:").
#
# This file exists empty on purpose. The gate scans all of history, so a single
# false positive - a test vector, a hex string that looks like a token - would
# otherwise fail every future pull request with no way to move on short of
# rewriting history or deleting the gate. Add the fingerprint here with a
# comment saying why it is not a secret.
#
# A *real* leak is not an entry here: rotate the credential first, then decide.
